.TH PATCHWHY 1
.SH NAME
patchwhy \\- observe executable or library restart evidence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B patchwhy
patchwhy --path PATH [--format json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Captures a current binary or library identity for restart analysis.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBpatchwhy --help\fR for the complete, version-specific flag list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses the shared CLI status convention: 0 success, 1 a completed negative finding or policy failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 a partial result, and 4 a runtime failure. Not every status applies to every command.
